{%- comment -%}
  Buy box, every part of the product page's buy column, in one place, so the
  product page and the quick-add drawer behave identically.

  Three ways to call it
    1. One main-product block (main-product loops its blocks):
         {% render 'buy-box', product: product, section: section, block: block, variant: current %}
    2. Compact, for chrome's quick-add-product section (Section Rendering):
         {% render 'buy-box', product: product, section: section, compact: true %}
       → variant picker, stock, Add button, one-line risk reversal. The drawer
         already shows the title and price above it, so those are off unless
         show_title: true / show_price: true are passed.
    3. A single named part: part: 'data' → the product JSON island product.js
       reads (main-product renders it once, outside the blocks).
       part: 'variant_id' → just the id of the variant to show (main-product
       captures it, so the page and quick add pick the same default).

  Parameters
    product, section   required
    block              a main-product block
    compact            true → the compact box (see above)
    variant            the variant to show; else ?variant= > most chosen > the
                       first available in size order (smallest first)
    part               'data' | 'variant_id' | 'flags'
    show_title         compact only
    show_price         compact only
    pending            true → no size chosen yet (audit PDP-09, main-product
                       works it out): "From £109", "Choose a size" on the
                       button, no size checked, no offer or stock line until
                       the shopper picks one (product.js), and the variant id
                       input empty so nothing is added by accident. `variant`
                       is still a real one (first available in size order):
                       the delivery dates and structured data use it.

  October 2026 audit blocks (snippets pdp-*): subtitle (tagline), offer,
  delivery (dated line, core delivery-estimate), trust_row (three promises,
  each opening a bottom sheet), benefits (custom.benefits, else bullets from
  the bed's metafields), spec_card ("What's inside"), worth_it, qa, story
  (the description, collapsed) and complete (one add-on, e.g. the stairs).

  Psychology (all honest, all switchable)
    - Price anchoring: compare-at struck through + "Save £X" (price snippet),
      per-night reframe with its basis one tap away, price inside the button.
    - Default effect: the merchant's most-chosen size is pre-selected server
      side; product.js upgrades that to the Bed Finder size when there is one.
    - Honest scarcity: "Only 3 left in Medium" ONLY when Shopify tracks the
      variant, it can't oversell (policy deny) and stock ≤ the low-stock setting.
    - Honest urgency: the dispatch countdown comes from the real cut-off.
    - Risk reversal sits directly under the button, for products the sleep
      trial covers (snippets/trial-eligible). Anything it doesn't cover gets
      a plain line saying so instead (custom.returns_note, or the standard
      wording), never the trial promise.
    - Made to order (personalised type/tags, tag made-to-order, or
      custom.lead_time_days): no dated dispatch countdown and no "ready to
      dispatch"; "Made to order: dispatched within N working days" instead.
    - Personalised products (type contains Personalised, tag personalised /
      personalised dog bed / personalisation:yes, or custom.personalisation_label;
      personalisation:no turns it off): a required name field inside the
      product form, so the order can always be made. Express checkout buttons
      are left off for them, so nothing skips the field.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product != blank and product.id != blank -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    ---- The selected variant (same rule as main-product) ----
  endcomment
  assign current = variant
  if current == blank or current.id == blank
    assign current = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    if product.selected_variant == blank and product.has_only_default_variant == false
      assign mc_found = false
      for v in product.variants
        if v.available and v.metafields.custom.most_chosen.value == true
          assign current = v
          assign mc_found = true
          break
        endif
      endfor
      assign mc_value = section.settings.most_chosen_value | default: '' | downcase | strip
      if mc_found == false and mc_value != ''
        for v in product.variants
          if v.available
            for o in v.options
              assign od = o | downcase | strip
              if od == mc_value
                assign current = v
                assign mc_found = true
                break
              endif
            endfor
          endif
          if mc_found
            break
          endif
        endfor
      endif
      comment
        No most chosen: the first available variant in size order (XS < S <
        M < L < XL…, snippets/size-hints), so a product whose variants were
        entered XL first doesn't open on its dearest size. Only when every
        size value has a rank; otherwise Shopify's own order stands.
      endcomment
      if mc_found == false
        assign sel_size_opt = nil
        assign sel_size_i = -1
        for option in product.options_with_values
          assign sel_on = option.name | downcase
          if sel_on contains 'size'
            assign sel_size_opt = option
            assign sel_size_i = forloop.index0
            break
          endif
        endfor
        if sel_size_i >= 0 and sel_size_opt.values.size > 1
          assign sel_keys = ''
          assign sel_ranked = true
          for sv in sel_size_opt.values
            assign sv_s = sv.name | default: sv | append: ''
            capture sv_parsed
              render 'size-hints', value: sv_s, mode: 'parse'
            endcapture
            assign sv_rank = sv_parsed | split: '|' | first | plus: 0
            if sv_rank < 1
              assign sel_ranked = false
              break
            endif
            assign sv_pos = forloop.index0 | plus: 100
            assign sv_key = sv_rank | plus: 100 | append: '~' | append: sv_pos
            assign sel_keys = sel_keys | append: sv_key | append: ','
          endfor
          if sel_ranked
            assign sel_sorted = sel_keys | split: ',' | sort
            assign sel_done = false
            for k in sel_sorted
              assign k_i = k | split: '~' | last | plus: 0 | minus: 100
              assign k_val = sel_size_opt.values[k_i]
              assign k_val = k_val.name | default: k_val | append: ''
              for v in product.variants
                if v.available and v.options[sel_size_i] == k_val
                  assign current = v
                  assign sel_done = true
                  break
                endif
              endfor
              if sel_done
                break
              endif
            endfor
          endif
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ---- Shared facts ----
  endcomment
  assign size_idx = -1
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign oname = option.name | downcase
    if oname contains 'size'
      assign size_idx = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign nights = settings.trial_nights | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign years = settings.guarantee_years | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign trial_on = false
  if settings.trial_enable and nights > 0
    assign trial_on = true
  endif
  comment
    Does the sleep trial cover THIS product? (snippets/trial-eligible: Theme
    settings → Promises → Not covered by the trial, and trial:yes / trial:no
    tags.) trial_on says the shop runs a trial; trial_ok says it applies here.
  endcomment
  assign trial_ok = false
  if trial_on
    capture bb_trial
      render 'trial-eligible', product: product
    endcapture
    if bb_trial == 'true'
      assign trial_ok = true
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Personalised (needs a name to be made) and made to order (no same-day
    dispatch promise).
  endcomment
  assign pers_label = product.metafields.custom.personalisation_label.value | default: '' | strip
  capture bb_pers
    render 'personalised', product: product
  endcapture
  assign is_personalised = false
  if bb_pers == 'true'
    assign is_personalised = true
  endif
  assign lead_days = product.metafields.custom.lead_time_days.value | default: 0 | plus: 0 | round
  comment
    The one made-to-order rule (snippets/product-fact made_to_order: personalised,
    lead days, or the made-to-order tag), shared with the FAQ, the trust-row
    sheet and the basket's delivery line.
  endcomment
  capture bb_mto
    render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'made_to_order'
  endcapture
  assign made_to_order = false
  if bb_mto == 'true'
    assign made_to_order = true
  endif
  if lead_days > 0
    assign made_text = 'product.made.lead' | t: days: lead_days
  else
    assign made_text = 'product.made.generic' | t
  endif

  comment
    What to say instead of the trial on a product it doesn't cover: the
    product's own custom.returns_note, else the standard wording (made to
    order with a name / not covered). Escaped, ready to print.
  endcomment
  assign excluded_note = ''
  if trial_on and trial_ok == false
    assign excluded_note = product.metafields.custom.returns_note.value | default: '' | strip | escape
    if excluded_note == ''
      if is_personalised
        assign excluded_note = 'product.risk.excluded_personalised' | t: nights: nights
      else
        assign excluded_note = 'product.risk.excluded' | t: nights: nights
      endif
    endif
  endif
  comment
    Returns wording from Theme settings → Promises (snippets/trial-terms),
    for the trial_terms and trial_terms_short tokens in block text.
  endcomment
  capture trial_terms
    render 'trial-terms'
  endcapture
  capture trial_terms_short
    render 'trial-terms', short: true
  endcapture
  assign ph_terms = trial_terms | escape
  assign ph_terms_short = trial_terms_short | escape
  comment
    One foam-bed test (snippets/foam-bed) for every foam-specific claim in
    the buy box: the guarantee is on the foam, so it (and the per-night
    reframe built on it) is only promised for a bed it covers (its
    description says so, or tag guarantee:yes), and the foam-describing
    tagline / benefits fallbacks only show on those beds.
  endcomment
  capture bb_foam
    render 'foam-bed', product: product
  endcapture
  assign is_foam = false
  if bb_foam == 'true'
    assign is_foam = true
  endif
  assign guarantee_on = false
  if settings.guarantee_enable and years > 0 and is_foam
    assign guarantee_on = true
  endif
  assign threshold_cents = 0
  if settings.free_shipping_enable and settings.free_shipping_threshold > 0
    assign threshold_cents = settings.free_shipping_threshold | times: 100 | round
  endif
  assign threshold_money = threshold_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
  comment
    Delivery choices under the Add button (snippets/delivery-options, Theme
    settings → Promises → Delivery options). When it's on, the stock line
    leaves out its own free-delivery note, so delivery is said once.
  endcomment
  assign delivery_line_on = false
  assign dl_std = settings.delivery_standard_text | default: '' | strip
  assign dl_exp = settings.delivery_express_text | default: '' | strip
  if dl_std != '' or dl_exp != ''
    assign delivery_line_on = true
  endif
  assign nights_s = nights | append: ''
  assign years_s = years | append: ''
  assign low_limit = 0
  if settings.low_stock_enable
    assign low_limit = settings.low_stock_threshold | default: 0 | plus: 0
  endif

  comment
    ---- Stock state of the selected variant ----
    in | low | backorder | out
  endcomment
  assign stock_state = 'in'
  assign stock_qty = current.inventory_quantity | default: 0 | plus: 0
  if current.available == false
    assign stock_state = 'out'
  elsif current.inventory_management == 'shopify' and current.inventory_policy == 'continue' and stock_qty <= 0
    assign stock_state = 'backorder'
  elsif low_limit > 0 and current.inventory_management == 'shopify' and current.inventory_policy == 'deny' and stock_qty > 0 and stock_qty <= low_limit
    assign stock_state = 'low'
  endif

  assign form_id = 'product-form-' | append: section.id
  if compact
    assign form_id = form_id | append: '-compact'
  endif

  comment
    ---- Which parts to render ----
  endcomment
  if part != blank
    assign parts = part | split: ','
  elsif compact
    assign parts_str = 'data'
    if show_title
      assign parts_str = parts_str | append: ',title'
    endif
    if show_price
      assign parts_str = parts_str | append: ',price'
    endif
    assign parts_str = parts_str | append: ',variant_picker,stock,buy_buttons,risk_reversal'
    assign parts = parts_str | split: ','
  else
    assign parts = block.type | split: ','
  endif

  assign bs = block.settings

  comment
    The bed's short name for headings and the WhatsApp message: "Coniston"
    from "Coniston Low-Entry Memory Foam Dog Bed", "Grasmere" from "The
    Grasmere Bolster Sofa Dog Bed". A generic first word keeps the title.
  endcomment
  assign full_title = product.title | split: ' | ' | first | strip
  assign short_name = full_title | remove_first: 'The ' | split: ' ' | first | default: full_title
  assign sn_lc = short_name | downcase
  if sn_lc == 'orthopaedic' or sn_lc == 'dog' or sn_lc == 'memory' or sn_lc == 'personalised' or sn_lc == 'luxury' or sn_lc == 'large' or sn_lc == 'small' or sn_lc == 'extra'
    assign short_name = full_title
  endif

  comment
    The quick add (compact) follows the same rule: sections/quick-add-product
    passes pending when a size must be chosen (audit PDP-09).
  endcomment
  assign is_pending = false
  if pending and product.has_only_default_variant == false
    assign is_pending = true
  endif
  assign has_offer_block = false
  assign has_delivery_block = false
  if compact != true
    for sb in section.blocks
      if sb.type == 'offer'
        assign has_offer_block = true
      elsif sb.type == 'delivery'
        assign has_delivery_block = true
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{%- if compact -%}
  <div class="buy-box buy-box--compact" data-product-scope data-section-id="{{ section.id }}" data-buy-box>
{%- endif -%}
{%- for p in parts -%}
  {%- case p -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- The default variant's id (main-product) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'variant_id' -%}
      {{- current.id -}}

    {%- comment -%}
      ---------- Facts for other product sections (product-timeline) ----------
      "trial|made|lead_days": trial 1 when the sleep trial covers this
      product, made 1 when it's made to order, lead_days its
      custom.lead_time_days (0 when unknown).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'flags' -%}
      {%- if trial_ok %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}|{% if made_to_order %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}|{{ lead_days -}}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- JSON island for product.js ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'data' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign colour_idx = -1
        for option in product.options_with_values
          assign oname = option.name | downcase
          if oname contains 'colour' or oname contains 'color'
            assign colour_idx = forloop.index0
            break
          endif
        endfor
        assign fallback_img = product.featured_media.preview_image
      -%}
      <script type="application/json" data-product-json>
        {
          "id": {{ product.id | json }},
          "handle": {{ product.handle | json }},
          "title": {{ product.title | json }},
          "url": {{ product.url | json }},
          "options": {{ product.options | json }},
          "sizeIndex": {{ size_idx }},
          "colourIndex": {{ colour_idx }},
          "onlyDefault": {{ product.has_only_default_variant | json }},
          "currentId": {% if is_pending %}null{% else %}{{ current.id | json }}{% endif %},
          "pending": {{ is_pending | json }},
          "shortName": {{ short_name | json }},
          "image": {% if fallback_img %}{{ fallback_img | image_url: width: 160 | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
          "variants": [
            {%- for v in product.variants -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign v_state = 'in'
                assign v_qty = v.inventory_quantity | default: 0 | plus: 0
                assign v_low = 'null'
                if v.available == false
                  assign v_state = 'out'
                elsif v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_policy == 'continue' and v_qty <= 0
                  assign v_state = 'backorder'
                elsif low_limit > 0 and v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_policy == 'deny' and v_qty > 0 and v_qty <= low_limit
                  assign v_state = 'low'
                  assign v_low = v_qty
                endif
                assign v_img = v.featured_media.preview_image
              -%}
              {
                "id": {{ v.id | json }},
                "title": {{ v.title | json }},
                "options": {{ v.options | json }},
                "available": {{ v.available | json }},
                "price": {{ v.price | json }},
                "compare_at_price": {{ v.compare_at_price | default: 0 | json }},
                "sku": {{ v.sku | default: '' | json }},
                "featured_media": {% if v.featured_media %}{"id": {{ v.featured_media.id | json }}, "src": {{ v_img | image_url: width: 160 | json }}}{% else %}null{% endif %},
                "most_chosen": {{ v.metafields.custom.most_chosen.value | default: false | json }},
                "stock": {"state": {{ v_state | json }}, "qty": {{ v_low }}}
              }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ],
          "strings": {
            "addPrice": {{ 'product.buy.add_price' | t: price: '[price]' | json }},
            "add": {{ 'product.buy.add' | t | json }},
            "preorderPrice": {{ 'product.buy.preorder_price' | t: price: '[price]' | json }},
            "preorder": {{ 'product.buy.preorder' | t | json }},
            "soldOut": {{ 'product.buy.sold_out' | t | json }},
            "unavailable": {{ 'product.buy.unavailable' | t | json }},
            "added": {{ 'product.buy.added' | t | json }},
            "viewBasket": {{ 'product.buy.view_basket' | t | json }},
            "error": {{ 'product.buy.error' | t | json }},
            "inStock": {{ 'product.stock.in_stock' | t | json }},
            "low": {{ 'product.stock.low' | t: count: '[count]', size: '[size]' | json }},
            "lowSingle": {{ 'product.stock.low_single' | t: count: '[count]' | json }},
            "backorder": {{ 'product.stock.backorder' | t | json }},
            "soldOutIn": {{ 'product.stock.sold_out' | t: size: '[size]' | json }},
            "soldOutSingle": {{ 'product.stock.sold_out_single' | t | json }},
            "valueSoldOut": {{ 'product.picker.sold_out' | t | json }},
            "valueUnavailable": {{ 'product.picker.unavailable' | t | json }},
            "status": {{ 'product.picker.status' | t | json }},
            "installments": {{ 'product.price.installments' | t: count: '[count]', amount: '[amount]', provider: '[provider]' | json }},
            "qualifies": {{ 'product.delivery.qualifies' | t | json }},
            "threshold": {{ 'product.delivery.threshold' | t: amount: '[amount]' | json }},
            "finderResult": {{ 'product.finder.result' | t | json }},
            "finderResultDefault": {{ 'product.finder.result_default' | t | json }},
            "wasPrice": {{ 'accessibility.was_price' | t | json }},
            "salePrice": {{ 'accessibility.sale_price' | t | json }},
            "regularPrice": {{ 'accessibility.regular_price' | t | json }},
            "save": {{ 'general.save' | t: amount: '[amount]' | json }},
            "priceSoldOut": {{ 'general.sold_out' | t | json }},
            "chooseSize": {{ 'product.buy.choose_size' | t | json }},
            "chooseSizeFirst": {{ 'product.buy.choose_size_first' | t | json }},
            "chooseSizeLegend": {{ 'product.picker.choose_size' | t | json }},
            "from": {{ 'general.from' | t | json }}
          }
        }
      </script>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Title + badges ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'title' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign h_class = bs.heading_size | default: 'h2'
        if compact
          assign h_class = 'h3'
        endif
        assign display_title = product.title
        unless bs.trim_title == false
          assign display_title = product.title | split: ' | ' | first
        endunless
        assign badge_list = ''
        unless bs.show_badges == false
          for tag in product.tags
            assign tl = tag | downcase
            assign p6 = tl | slice: 0, 6
            if p6 == 'badge:'
              assign b_txt = tag | slice: 6, 60 | strip | remove: '|'
              if b_txt != ''
                assign badge_list = badge_list | append: b_txt | append: '|'
              endif
            endif
          endfor
        endunless
        assign badges = badge_list | split: '|'
      -%}
      <div class="pblock pblock--title"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
        {%- if badges.size > 0 or settings.finder_enable -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The finder's match badge is revealed by global.js after load, so it
            goes last (it never pushes the merchant's badges along), and on the
            matched bed the row is kept open from first paint (the <head>
            script sets html[data-finder-handle]), so the title doesn't drop.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if settings.finder_enable -%}
            {%- style -%}
              html[data-finder-handle="{{ product.handle | escape }}"] .buy-box__badges[data-finder-match-handle="{{ product.handle | escape }}"] { display: flex; min-height: var(--badge-row-h, 1.625rem); }
            {%- endstyle -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="buy-box__badges" data-finder-match-handle="{{ product.handle }}">
            {%- for b in badges limit: 3 -%}
              {%- if forloop.first -%}
                {%- render 'badge', text: b, style: 'accent' -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- render 'badge', text: b -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- if settings.finder_enable -%}
              <span class="badge badge--match" data-finder-match-badge hidden>
                {%- render 'icon', name: 'paw' -%}
                <span data-finder-name="{{ 'product.title.match' | t }}">{{ 'product.title.match_default' | t }}</span>
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if compact -%}
          <h2 class="buy-box__title {{ h_class }}">{{ display_title | escape }}</h2>
        {%- else -%}
          <h1 class="buy-box__title {{ h_class }}" id="ProductTitle-{{ section.id }}">{{ display_title | escape }}</h1>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Rating (real reviews only) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'rating' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign show_count = true
        if bs.show_count == false
          assign show_count = false
        endif
      -%}
      {%- capture rating_html -%}{%- render 'rating', product: product, size: 'md', show_count: show_count -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if rating_html != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--rating"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          {%- if bs.link_to_reviews == false -%}
            {{ rating_html }}
          {%- else -%}
            <a href="#reviews" class="buy-box__rating-link" data-reviews-link>
              {{ rating_html }}
              <span class="buy-box__rating-cta">{{ 'product.rating.link' | t }}</span>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- elsif request.design_mode and block -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--rating pblock--editor-note" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <p class="small muted">{{ 'product.rating.editor_note' | t }}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      ---------- Subtitle (block type 'tagline') ----------
      One line under the title saying what the bed physically does (audit
      PDP-04, S05): custom.subtitle, else the older custom.tagline
      (snippets/product-fact), else the block's fallback text only when the
      merchant has written one, else nothing.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'tagline' -%}
      {%- liquid
        capture tagline
          render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'subtitle'
        endcapture
        assign tagline = tagline | strip
        assign tagline_escaped = true
        if tagline == ''
          assign tagline_escaped = false
          comment
            The fallback copy describes a memory-foam bed: by default it is
            only used on beds the foam guarantee covers (snippets/foam-bed:
            the description promises a no-flatten guarantee, or tag
            guarantee:yes).
          endcomment
          if is_foam or bs.fallback_scope == 'all'
            assign tagline = bs.text | default: '' | strip
          endif
        endif
        assign tagline = tagline | replace: '[trial_nights]', nights_s | replace: '[guarantee_years]', years_s | replace: '[threshold]', threshold_money | replace: '[trial_terms_short]', trial_terms_short | replace: '[trial_terms]', trial_terms
      -%}
      {%- if tagline != '' -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--tagline"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          <p class="buy-box__tagline buy-box__tagline--{{ bs.style | default: 'serif' }}">{% if tagline_escaped %}{{ tagline }}{% else %}{{ tagline | escape }}{% endif %}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Price, per-night, instalments ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'price' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign show_pn = true
        if bs.show_per_night == false
          assign show_pn = false
        endif
        assign show_inst = false
        assign provider = settings.installments_provider | default: '' | strip
        if settings.show_installments and provider != ''
          unless bs.show_installments == false
            assign show_inst = true
          endunless
        endif
        assign inst_count = settings.installments_count | default: 3 | plus: 0
        if inst_count < 2
          assign inst_count = 2
        endif
      -%}
      {%- liquid
        comment
          No size chosen yet: "From £109" and the per-night sum for that
          price (PDF S05: "From £109 · About 6p a night…"); both follow the
          size once one is picked (product.js, global.js).
        endcomment
        assign pn_price = current.price
        if is_pending
          assign pn_price = product.price_min
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="pblock pblock--price"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
        <div class="buy-box__price" data-price-wrap>
          {%- if is_pending -%}
            {%- render 'price', product: product, size: 'lg', show_from: true, show_save: true, show_sold_out: false -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- render 'price', product: product, variant: current, size: 'lg', show_from: false, show_save: true, show_sold_out: false -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- if show_pn -%}
          {%- render 'per-night', price: pn_price, product: product, class: 'buy-box__per-night' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if show_inst -%}
          {%- assign inst_amount = current.price | divided_by: inst_count | money_without_trailing_zeros -%}
          <p class="buy-box__installments" data-installments data-count="{{ inst_count }}" data-provider="{{ provider | escape }}">
            {{- 'product.price.installments' | t: count: inst_count, amount: inst_amount, provider: provider -}}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if bs.show_tax_note -%}
          <p class="buy-box__tax">{{ 'product.price.tax_included' | t }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The running offer (Theme settings → Offer): the price this size
          really comes to at checkout, or which size reaches the minimum.
          product.js keeps it in step with the size and the basket.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- unless has_offer_block -%}
          {%- capture offer_html -%}
            {%- render 'offer', mode: 'pdp', product: product, variant: current, cart: cart, class: 'buy-box__offer' -%}
          {%- endcapture -%}
          {%- if is_pending -%}
            {%- assign offer_html = offer_html | replace: 'data-state="none"', 'data-state="none" data-offer-pending' | replace: 'data-state="line"', 'data-state="none" data-offer-pending hidden' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {{- offer_html -}}
        {%- endunless -%}
      </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      ---------- The offer, for the size picked (block type 'offer') ----------
      Core snippets/offer mode pdp: "£15 off this size at checkout, until Sat
      31 Oct", only for a size that qualifies (PDP-07). Before a size is
      chosen it is printed hidden, and global.js shows it once a qualifying
      size is picked (Lunova.offer.update on lunova:variant:change).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'offer' -%}
      {%- capture offer_html -%}
        {%- render 'offer', mode: 'pdp', product: product, variant: current, cart: cart, class: 'buy-box__offer' -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if offer_html != blank -%}
        {%- if is_pending -%}
          {%- assign offer_html = offer_html | replace: 'data-state="none"', 'data-state="none" data-offer-pending' | replace: 'data-state="line"', 'data-state="none" data-offer-pending hidden' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--offer"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          {{- offer_html -}}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Variant picker ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'variant_picker' -%}
      {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--variant_picker"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          {%- liquid
            assign update_url = true
            if compact
              assign update_url = false
            endif
            render 'variant-picker', product: product, section: section, variant: current, block: block, compact: compact, update_url: update_url, pending: is_pending
          -%}
          {%- if compact != true and bs.show_size_help != false -%}
            {%- render 'pdp-size-help', product: product, short_name: short_name, whatsapp: bs.whatsapp_number -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endunless -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Honest stock line ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'stock' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign show_in = true
        if bs.show_in_stock == false
          assign show_in = false
        endif
        assign in_text = bs.in_stock_text | default: '' | strip | escape
        if in_text == ''
          assign in_text = 'product.stock.in_stock' | t
        endif
        comment
          Made to order: "ready to dispatch" isn't true, so the in-stock line
          says how it's made and when it goes out instead.
        endcomment
        if made_to_order
          assign in_text = made_text
          assign show_in = true
        endif

        comment
          The size by its own name, as the picker shows it in bold: Large,
          not Large · 91 × 69 × 24cm or the breed list after a colon.
        endcomment
        assign size_label = ''
        if size_idx >= 0
          assign size_val = current.options[size_idx]
          capture size_label
            render 'size-hints', value: size_val, mode: 'size_label'
          endcapture
          assign size_label = size_label | strip | default: size_val
          assign sl_lc = size_label | downcase
          if sl_lc == size_label
            assign size_label = size_label | capitalize
          endif
        elsif product.has_only_default_variant == false
          assign size_label = current.title
        endif

        case stock_state
          when 'low'
            if size_label != ''
              assign stock_text = 'product.stock.low' | t: count: stock_qty, size: size_label
            else
              assign stock_text = 'product.stock.low_single' | t: count: stock_qty
            endif
          when 'backorder'
            assign stock_text = 'product.stock.backorder' | t
          when 'out'
            if size_label != ''
              assign stock_text = 'product.stock.sold_out' | t: size: size_label
            else
              assign stock_text = 'product.stock.sold_out_single' | t
            endif
          else
            assign stock_text = in_text
        endcase

        comment
          Stock and delivery on one line (block setting show_delivery): the
          dispatch estimate from delivery-promise, kept live by global.js from
          the real cut-off, follows the stock status directly above the
          button. Hidden while the variant is sold out or on back order, as
          in the Delivery block.
        endcomment
        assign with_delivery = false
        assign sl_promise = ''
        assign sl_free = false
        if bs.show_delivery
          assign with_delivery = true
          comment
            No dated countdown on a made-to-order product: the stock line
            already says when it's dispatched.
          endcomment
          unless made_to_order
            capture sl_promise
              render 'delivery-promise', variant: current
            endcapture
          endunless
          if threshold_cents > 0 and delivery_line_on == false
            unless bs.show_free_delivery_note == false
              assign sl_free = true
            endunless
          endif
        endif
        assign sl_hide_delivery = false
        if stock_state == 'out' or stock_state == 'backorder'
          assign sl_hide_delivery = true
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="pblock pblock--stock{% if with_delivery %} pblock--stock-line{% endif %}"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
        {%- if with_delivery -%}<div class="stock-line">{%- endif -%}
        <p
          class="stock stock--{{ stock_state }}"
          data-stock
          data-in-stock-text="{{ in_text }}"
          data-show-in-stock="{{ show_in }}"
          {%- if is_pending and stock_state != 'out' %} hidden{% elsif stock_state == 'in' and show_in == false %} hidden{% endif %}
        >
          <span class="stock__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="stock__text" data-stock-text>{{ stock_text }}</span>
        </p>
        {%- if with_delivery -%}
          {%- if sl_promise != blank or sl_free -%}
            <div class="stock-line__delivery" data-delivery-wrap{% if sl_hide_delivery %} hidden{% endif %}>
              {{- sl_promise -}}
              {%- if sl_free -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign sl_qualifies = false
                  if current.price >= threshold_cents
                    assign sl_qualifies = true
                  endif
                -%}
                <span class="stock-line__free{% if sl_qualifies %} is-qualified{% endif %}" data-free-delivery data-threshold="{{ threshold_cents }}">
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'check-circle', class: 'stock-line__free-icon' -%}
                  <span data-free-delivery-text>
                    {%- if sl_qualifies -%}{{ 'product.delivery.qualifies' | t }}{%- else -%}{{ 'product.delivery.threshold' | t: amount: threshold_money }}{%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      ---------- Delivery dates (block type 'delivery') ----------
      The bed's own dated line (audit P0-3, PDP-11), from core
      snippets/delivery-estimate: own stock "Free standard delivery: arrives
      Thu 15 Oct to Mon 19 Oct" (+ Express); partner warehouse with no
      dispatch days: no dates, the partner wording. Never same-day dispatch
      unless custom.ships_same_day (the countdown stays a core setting).
      Made to order: "Made to order: dispatched within N working days" too.
      Hidden while the size is sold out or on back order.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'delivery' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign hide_delivery = false
        if stock_state == 'out' or stock_state == 'backorder'
          assign hide_delivery = true
        endif
        if is_pending
          assign hide_delivery = false
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="pblock pblock--delivery"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
        <div class="buy-box__delivery" data-delivery-wrap{% if hide_delivery %} hidden{% endif %}>
          {%- liquid
            comment
              Made to order: the policy's 1 to 2 day dispatch doesn't hold, so
              no dates unless the product's own dispatch days are set; the
              standard delivery terms instead.
            endcomment
            capture mto_dated
              render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'dated'
            endcapture
          -%}
          {%- if made_to_order -%}
            <p class="buy-box__made">
              {%- render 'icon', name: 'clock', class: 'buy-box__made-icon' -%}
              <span>{{ made_text }}</span>
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if made_to_order and mto_dated != 'true' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign mto_std = settings.delivery_standard_price | default: '' | strip | remove: '£' | times: 100 | round | money_without_trailing_zeros
              assign mto_min = settings.delivery_min_days | default: 4 | plus: 0
              assign mto_max = settings.delivery_max_days | default: 6 | plus: 0
            -%}
            <p class="buy-box__made">
              {%- render 'icon', name: 'truck', class: 'buy-box__made-icon' -%}
              <span>{{ 'product.trust_row.delivery_standard' | t: amount: threshold_money, price: mto_std, min: mto_min, max: mto_max }}</span>
            </p>
          {%- else -%}
            {%- render 'delivery-estimate', product: product, variant: current, class: 'buy-box__delivery-estimate' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Product form ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'buy_buttons' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign show_qty = false
        if bs.show_quantity
          assign show_qty = true
        endif
        assign price_in_button = true
        if bs.show_price_in_button == false
          assign price_in_button = false
        endif
        assign show_dynamic = true
        if bs.show_dynamic_checkout == false or compact or is_personalised
          assign show_dynamic = false
        endif
        assign show_terms = true
        if bs.show_payment_terms == false or compact
          assign show_terms = false
        endif

        assign price_money = current.price | money_without_trailing_zeros
        if is_pending
          assign btn_label = 'product.buy.choose_size' | t
        elsif current.available == false
          assign btn_label = 'product.buy.sold_out' | t
        elsif stock_state == 'backorder'
          if price_in_button
            assign btn_label = 'product.buy.preorder_price' | t: price: price_money
          else
            assign btn_label = 'product.buy.preorder' | t
          endif
        elsif price_in_button
          assign btn_label = 'product.buy.add_price' | t: price: price_money
        else
          assign btn_label = 'product.buy.add' | t
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="pblock pblock--buy_buttons"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
        <product-form
          class="product-form"
          data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
          data-price-in-button="{{ price_in_button }}"
          {%- if compact %} data-compact{% endif %}
          {%- if is_pending %} data-pending{% endif %}
        >
          {%- comment -%}
            No novalidate here: without JavaScript the browser itself stops a
            personalised bed going in without its name. product.js switches
            native validation off and checks the field itself.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- form 'product', product, id: form_id, class: 'product-form__form', data-product-form: '' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              No size chosen yet: the id stays empty (and disabled, so without
              JavaScript the noscript select below is what posts).
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{% unless is_pending %}{{ current.id }}{% endunless %}" data-variant-id-input{% if is_pending %} disabled{% endif %}>
            {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
              <noscript>
                <div class="product-form__noscript field">
                  <label class="field__label" for="{{ form_id }}-select">{{ 'product.picker.noscript_label' | t }}</label>
                  <select class="select" id="{{ form_id }}-select" name="id">
                    {%- for v in product.variants -%}
                      <option value="{{ v.id }}"{% if v.id == current.id %} selected{% endif %}{% unless v.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
                        {{- v.title | escape }} · {{ v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
                        {%- unless v.available %} ({{ 'product.buy.sold_out' | t }}){% endunless -%}
                      </option>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </select>
                </div>
              </noscript>
            {%- endunless -%}

            {%- if is_personalised -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign pers_max = product.metafields.custom.personalisation_max_length.value | default: 15 | plus: 0 | round
                if pers_max < 1
                  assign pers_max = 15
                endif
                if pers_label != ''
                  assign pers_field_label = pers_label | escape
                  assign pers_key = pers_label | escape
                else
                  assign pers_field_label = 'product.personalise.label' | t
                  assign pers_key = 'product.personalise.property' | t
                endif
                assign pers_id = form_id | append: '-personalise'
              -%}
              <div class="personalise field" data-personalise>
                <label class="field__label personalise__label" for="{{ pers_id }}">
                  {{- pers_field_label }} <span class="personalise__req">{{ 'product.personalise.required_marker' | t }}</span>
                </label>
                <input
                  class="input personalise__input"
                  type="text"
                  id="{{ pers_id }}"
                  name="properties[{{ pers_key }}]"
                  maxlength="{{ pers_max }}"
                  required
                  aria-required="true"
                  autocomplete="off"
                  autocapitalize="words"
                  spellcheck="false"
                  aria-describedby="{{ pers_id }}-hint"
                  data-personalise-input
                >
                <p class="field__hint personalise__hint" id="{{ pers_id }}-hint">{{ 'product.personalise.hint' | t: max: pers_max }}</p>
                <p class="field__error personalise__error" id="{{ pers_id }}-error" data-personalise-error data-message="{{ 'product.personalise.error' | t }}" role="alert" hidden></p>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if show_qty -%}
              <div class="product-form__qty field">
                <label class="field__label" for="{{ form_id }}-qty">{{ 'product.buy.quantity' | t }}</label>
                <div class="qty" data-qty>
                  <button type="button" class="qty__btn" data-qty-step="-1" aria-label="{{ 'product.buy.decrease' | t }}">
                    {%- render 'icon', name: 'minus' -%}
                  </button>
                  <input
                    class="qty__input"
                    type="number"
                    id="{{ form_id }}-qty"
                    name="quantity"
                    value="1"
                    min="1"
                    inputmode="numeric"
                    data-qty-input
                  >
                  <button type="button" class="qty__btn" data-qty-step="1" aria-label="{{ 'product.buy.increase' | t }}">
                    {%- render 'icon', name: 'plus' -%}
                  </button>
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="product-form__buttons">
              <button
                type="submit"
                name="add"
                class="btn btn--primary btn--lg btn--block product-form__submit"
                data-add-button
                {%- if is_pending %} aria-describedby="{{ form_id }}-size-error"{% elsif current.available == false %} disabled{% endif %}
              >
                <span data-add-label>{{ btn_label }}</span>
              </button>
              {%- if show_dynamic -%}
                <div class="product-form__dynamic" data-dynamic-checkout{% if is_pending or current.available == false %} hidden{% endif %}>
                  {{ form | payment_button }}
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            {%- if is_pending -%}
              <p class="product-form__error product-form__size-error" id="{{ form_id }}-size-error" data-size-error role="alert" hidden></p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <div class="product-form__message" data-form-message role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
            <p class="product-form__error" data-form-error role="alert" hidden></p>

            {%- if show_terms -%}
              <div class="product-form__terms">{{ form | payment_terms }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endform -%}
        </product-form>
        {%- if delivery_line_on and has_delivery_block == false -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign dl_hide = false
            if stock_state == 'out' or stock_state == 'backorder'
              assign dl_hide = true
            endif
          -%}
          <div class="buy-box__delivery-options" data-delivery-wrap{% if dl_hide %} hidden{% endif %}>
            {%- render 'delivery-options', product: product, variant: current, price: current.price, compact: compact -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Compact: the one-line risk reversal rides with the button, so the
          two stay together when the button sticks to the drawer's bottom edge.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if compact and parts contains 'risk_reversal' -%}
          {%- if trial_ok -%}
            <p class="buy-box__risk-line">
              {%- render 'icon', name: 'moon' -%}
              <span>{{ 'core.trust.trial_title' | t: nights: nights }} · {{ 'core.trust.trial_sub' | t: terms_short: trial_terms_short }}</span>
            </p>
          {%- elsif excluded_note != '' -%}
            <p class="buy-box__risk-line buy-box__risk-line--note">
              {%- render 'icon', name: 'info' -%}
              <span>{{ excluded_note }}</span>
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Risk reversal, directly under the button ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'risk_reversal' -%}
      {%- if compact -%}
        {%- comment -%} Rendered inside the buy_buttons part (see above). {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign rr_heading = bs.heading | default: '' | replace: '[trial_nights]', nights_s | replace: '[guarantee_years]', years_s | replace: '[threshold]', threshold_money | replace: '[trial_terms_short]', trial_terms_short | replace: '[trial_terms]', trial_terms
          assign rr_text = bs.text | default: '' | replace: '[trial_nights]', nights_s | replace: '[guarantee_years]', years_s | replace: '[threshold]', threshold_money | replace: '[trial_terms_short]', trial_terms_short | replace: '[trial_terms]', trial_terms
          assign show_g = false
          if guarantee_on and bs.show_guarantee
            assign show_g = true
          endif
          assign returns_url = shop.refund_policy.url | default: ''
        -%}
        {%- if trial_on or show_g -%}
          <div class="pblock pblock--risk_reversal"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
            <div class="risk-reversal{% unless trial_ok %} risk-reversal--note{% endunless %}">
              {%- if trial_ok -%}
                <div class="risk-reversal__main">
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'moon', class: 'risk-reversal__icon' -%}
                  <p class="risk-reversal__text">
                    {%- if rr_heading != '' -%}<strong class="risk-reversal__heading">{{ rr_heading | escape }}</strong> {% endif -%}
                    {{- rr_text | escape -}}
                    {%- if returns_url != '' and bs.link_label != blank %}
                      <a class="risk-reversal__link" href="{{ returns_url }}">{{ bs.link_label | escape }}</a>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </p>
                </div>
              {%- elsif excluded_note != '' -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  The trial doesn't cover this product (kennels, personalised
                  beds…): say so plainly, where the promise would have been.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <div class="risk-reversal__main">
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'info', class: 'risk-reversal__icon' -%}
                  <p class="risk-reversal__text" data-trial-excluded>
                    {{- excluded_note -}}
                    {%- if returns_url != '' and bs.link_label != blank %}
                      <a class="risk-reversal__link" href="{{ returns_url }}">{{ bs.link_label | escape }}</a>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </p>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if show_g -%}
                <p class="risk-reversal__guarantee">
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'shield', class: 'risk-reversal__g-icon' -%}
                  <span>{{ 'product.risk.guarantee' | t: years: years }}</span>
                </p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Trust row + payment marks ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'trust' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign t_items = bs.items | default: 'secure' | remove: ' '
        capture trust_html
          render 'trust-list', items: t_items, layout: 'row', size: 'sm', class: 'buy-box__trust-list', for_product: product
        endcapture
        assign show_pay = true
        if bs.show_payment_icons == false
          assign show_pay = false
        endif
        if show_pay
          capture pay_html
            render 'payment-icons', class: 'buy-box__payments', limit: 8
          endcapture
        else
          assign pay_html = ''
        endif
      -%}
      {%- liquid
        comment
          Who you're buying from, and how you can pay, owner-entered (Theme
          settings → Social proof → Who you are). The payment line only while
          Shopify has no payment marks to show.
        endcomment
        assign pay_text = ''
        if show_pay and pay_html == blank
          assign pay_text = settings.payment_methods_text | default: '' | strip
        endif
        assign contact_line = settings.trust_contact_line | default: '' | strip
        assign contact_url = pages.contact.url | default: ''
      -%}
      {%- if trust_html != blank or pay_html != blank or pay_text != '' or contact_line != '' -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--trust"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          <div class="buy-box__trust">
            {{ trust_html }}
            {{ pay_html }}
            {%- if pay_text != '' -%}
              <p class="trust-note buy-box__pay-text">{%- render 'icon', name: 'lock' -%}<span>{{ pay_text | escape }}</span></p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if contact_line != '' -%}
              <p class="trust-note buy-box__contact">
                {%- render 'icon', name: 'chat' -%}
                {%- if contact_url != '' -%}
                  <a href="{{ contact_url }}">{{ contact_line | escape }}</a>
                {%- else -%}
                  <span>{{ contact_line | escape }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      ---------- Bullets (block type 'benefits') ----------
      "Why Coniston" (PDP-15): custom.benefits as written, else bullets
      built from the bed's own metafields (snippets/pdp-bullets), never a
      store-wide list. The block's fallback text only shows when the
      merchant has written one, and by default only on foam-guarantee beds.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'benefits' -%}
      {%- liquid
        capture bullets_html
          render 'pdp-bullets', product: product
        endcapture
        assign fallback = bs.content | default: ''
        if bullets_html != blank
          assign fallback = ''
        elsif bs.fallback_scope != 'all' and is_foam == false
          assign fallback = ''
        endif
        assign short_esc = short_name | escape
        assign b_heading = bs.heading | default: '' | escape | replace: '[name]', short_esc
      -%}
      {%- if bullets_html != blank or fallback != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--benefits"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          {%- if b_heading != '' -%}
            <h2 class="buy-box__benefits-heading">{{ b_heading }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if bullets_html != blank -%}
            <ul class="benefits" role="list">{{ bullets_html }}</ul>
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="benefits benefits--rte rte">
              {{- fallback | replace: '[trial_nights]', nights_s | replace: '[guarantee_years]', years_s | replace: '[threshold]', threshold_money | replace: '[trial_terms_short]', ph_terms_short | replace: '[trial_terms]', ph_terms -}}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Trust row with its sheets (PDP-13) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'trust_row' -%}
      {%- capture trust_row_html -%}{%- render 'pdp-trust-row', product: product, section: section, block: block -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if trust_row_html != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--trust_row"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          {{- trust_row_html -}}
          {%- liquid
            comment
              The owner line (PDP-25) beside the trust row, on beds without
              their own Q&A (the Q&A block carries it otherwise).
            endcomment
            capture tr_qa
              render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'qa_count'
            endcapture
          -%}
          {%- if bs.owner_line != blank and tr_qa == '0' -%}
            <p class="pdp-owner-line">{{ bs.owner_line | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- What's inside (PDP-16) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'spec_card' -%}
      {%- capture spec_html -%}{%- render 'pdp-spec-card', product: product, short_name: short_name, heading: bs.heading, intro: bs.intro -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if spec_html != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--spec_card"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>{{ spec_html }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Is it worth it? (PDP-17, custom.worth_it) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'worth_it' -%}
      {%- capture worth_html -%}{%- render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'worth_it' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if worth_html != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--worth_it"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          <div class="pdp-worth">
            <h2 class="h4 pdp-worth__heading">{{ bs.heading | default: 'Worth it?' | escape }}</h2>
            <p class="pdp-worth__text">{{ worth_html }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Questions owners ask (PDP-22, custom.qa) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'qa' -%}
      {%- capture qa_html -%}{%- render 'pdp-qa', product: product, heading: bs.heading, signature: bs.signature, owner_line: bs.owner_line -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if qa_html != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--qa"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>{{ qa_html }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- The story: description, collapsed (PDP-17) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'story' -%}
      {%- if product.description != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--story"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          {%- render 'pdp-story', product: product, heading: bs.heading, section: section -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Complete their bed (PDP-23) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'complete' -%}
      {%- capture complete_html -%}{%- render 'pdp-complete', product: product, addon: bs.product, heading: bs.heading, note: bs.note, show_on: bs.show_on -%}{%- render 'pdp-also-suits', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if complete_html != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--complete"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>{{ complete_html }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Bed Finder prompt / recommendation ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'finder_prompt' -%}
      {%- if settings.finder_enable -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign fp_heading = bs.heading | default: ''
          if fp_heading == ''
            assign fp_heading = 'product.finder.prompt_default' | t
          endif
          assign fp_cta = bs.cta_label | default: ''
          if fp_cta == ''
            assign fp_cta = 'product.finder.cta' | t
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--finder_prompt"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          <div class="finder-prompt" data-finder-prompt>
            {%- render 'icon', name: 'paw', class: 'finder-prompt__icon' -%}
            <div class="finder-prompt__body" data-finder-prompt-default>
              <p class="finder-prompt__heading">
                <span data-finder-name="{{ 'product.finder.prompt' | t }}">{{ fp_heading | escape }}</span>
              </p>
              <button type="button" class="finder-prompt__cta link" data-open-finder>
                {{- fp_cta | escape -}}
                {%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right' -%}
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="finder-prompt__body" data-finder-prompt-result hidden>
              <p class="finder-prompt__heading" data-finder-result-text></p>
              <p class="finder-prompt__note">
                {{ 'product.finder.result_note' | t }}
                <button type="button" class="link finder-prompt__retake" data-open-finder data-finder-step="1">{{ 'product.finder.retake' | t }}</button>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Size guide trigger (dialog: size-guide snippet) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'size_guide' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign sg_label = bs.label | default: ''
        if sg_label == ''
          assign sg_label = 'product.size_guide.open' | t
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="pblock pblock--size_guide"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
        <div class="size-guide-trigger">
          {%- render 'icon', name: 'ruler', class: 'size-guide-trigger__icon' -%}
          <p class="size-guide-trigger__text">
            {%- if bs.teaser != blank -%}<span class="size-guide-trigger__teaser">{{ bs.teaser | escape }}</span> {% endif -%}
            <button type="button" class="link size-guide-trigger__btn" data-size-guide-open aria-haspopup="dialog">{{ sg_label | escape }}</button>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Accordion row ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'accordion' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign src = bs.source | default: 'custom'
        assign extra = bs.content | default: ''
      -%}
      {%- if src == 'size_guide' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A row like the others that opens the size guide sheet (PDP-19)
          instead of folding open, on products with sizes to choose from.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if size_idx >= 0 and product.options_with_values[size_idx].values.size > 1 -%}
          <div class="pblock pblock--accordion"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
            <button type="button" class="product-accordion product-accordion--button" data-size-guide-open aria-haspopup="dialog">
              <span class="product-accordion__title">
                {%- if bs.icon != blank and bs.icon != 'none' -%}
                  {%- render 'icon', name: bs.icon, class: 'product-accordion__icon' -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                <span>{{ bs.heading | default: 'Size guide' | escape }}</span>
              </span>
              {%- render 'icon', name: 'chevron-right', class: 'product-accordion__go' -%}
            </button>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- capture acc_body -%}
        {%- case src -%}
          {%- when 'description' -%}
            {{- product.description -}}
          {%- when 'specs' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign spec_mf = product.metafields.custom.specs
              assign spec_raw = ''
              if spec_mf != blank and spec_mf.value != blank
                if spec_mf.type contains 'list.'
                  assign spec_raw = spec_mf.value | join: '<<>>'
                else
                  assign spec_raw = spec_mf.value | newline_to_br | replace: '<br />', '<<>>' | replace: '<br>', '<<>>'
                endif
              endif
              assign spec_lines = spec_raw | split: '<<>>'
            -%}
            {%- if spec_lines.size > 0 -%}
              <dl class="spec-list">
                {%- for line in spec_lines -%}
                  {%- assign l = line | strip -%}
                  {%- if l == '' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if l contains ':' -%}
                    {%- assign s_label = l | split: ':' | first | strip -%}
                    {%- assign s_value = l | remove_first: s_label | remove_first: ':' | strip -%}
                    <div class="spec-list__row">
                      <dt>{{ s_label | escape }}</dt>
                      <dd>{{ s_value | escape }}</dd>
                    </div>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <div class="spec-list__row spec-list__row--note"><dd>{{ l | escape }}</dd></div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- if current.sku != blank -%}
                  <div class="spec-list__row"><dt>SKU</dt><dd>{{ current.sku | escape }}</dd></div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </dl>
            {%- endif -%}
            {{- extra -}}
          {%- when 'delivery' -%}
            {%- liquid
              comment
                The published delivery policy, said once (PDP-18): dispatch,
                Standard and Express times and prices (Theme settings →
                Promises → Delivery dates), the free-delivery amount, and the
                partner warehouse note on partner beds. The trial and the
                guarantee have their own rows and sheets, so they aren't
                repeated here.
              endcomment
              assign df_dmin = settings.delivery_dispatch_min | default: 1 | plus: 0
              assign df_dmax = settings.delivery_dispatch_max | default: 2 | plus: 0
              assign df_tmin = settings.delivery_min_days | default: 4 | plus: 0
              assign df_tmax = settings.delivery_max_days | default: 6 | plus: 0
              assign df_xmin = settings.delivery_express_min | default: 2 | plus: 0
              assign df_xmax = settings.delivery_express_max | default: 3 | plus: 0
              assign df_std = settings.delivery_standard_price | default: '' | strip | remove: '£' | times: 100 | round | money_without_trailing_zeros
              assign df_exp_c = settings.delivery_express_price | default: '' | strip | remove: '£' | times: 100 | round
              assign df_exp = df_exp_c | money_without_trailing_zeros
              capture df_partner
                render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'partner'
              endcapture
            -%}
            <ul class="delivery-facts" role="list">
              {%- if made_to_order -%}
                <li>
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'clock', class: 'delivery-facts__icon' -%}
                  <span>{{ made_text }}</span>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if df_partner == 'true' -%}
                {%- capture df_dated -%}{%- render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'dated' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                <li>{%- render 'icon', name: 'truck', class: 'delivery-facts__icon' -%}<span>{% if df_dated == 'true' %}{{ 'product.trust_row.delivery_partner_dated' | t }}{% else %}{{ 'product.trust_row.delivery_partner' | t }}{% endif %}</span></li>
              {%- elsif made_to_order == false -%}
                <li>{%- render 'icon', name: 'clock', class: 'delivery-facts__icon' -%}<span>{{ 'product.trust_row.delivery_dispatch' | t: min: df_dmin, max: df_dmax }}</span></li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if threshold_cents > 0 -%}
                <li>{%- render 'icon', name: 'truck', class: 'delivery-facts__icon' -%}<span>{{ 'product.trust_row.delivery_standard' | t: amount: threshold_money, price: df_std, min: df_tmin, max: df_tmax }}</span></li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if settings.delivery_express_enable and df_exp_c > 0 and df_partner != 'true' -%}
                <li>{%- render 'icon', name: 'truck', class: 'delivery-facts__icon' -%}<span>{{ 'product.trust_row.delivery_express' | t: price: df_exp, min: df_xmin, max: df_xmax }}</span></li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if trial_on and trial_ok == false and excluded_note != '' -%}
                <li>{%- render 'icon', name: 'info', class: 'delivery-facts__icon' -%}<span>{{ excluded_note }}</span></li>
              {%- endif -%}
            </ul>
            {{- extra -}}
            {%- if shop.shipping_policy.url != blank or shop.refund_policy.url != blank -%}
              <p class="delivery-facts__links">
                {%- if shop.shipping_policy.url != blank -%}
                  <a href="{{ shop.shipping_policy.url }}">{{ 'product.accordion.shipping_policy' | t }}</a>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if shop.refund_policy.url != blank -%}
                  <a href="{{ shop.refund_policy.url }}">{{ 'product.accordion.refund_policy' | t }}</a>
                {%- endif -%}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- when 'guarantee' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Guarantee terms (PDP-17), only on beds the foam guarantee covers.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if guarantee_on -%}
              <p>{{ 'product.accordion.guarantee_terms' | t: years: years }}</p>
              {%- if shop.refund_policy.url != blank -%}
                <p><a href="{{ shop.refund_policy.url }}">{{ 'product.trust_row.full_terms' | t }}</a></p>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- when 'care' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign care_mf = product.metafields.custom.care
              comment
                No custom.care: say what the bed's own data does say about
                its cover (custom.cover_type, custom.wash_temp), else the
                block's text.
              endcomment
              capture care_cover
                render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'cover_type'
              endcapture
              capture care_wash
                render 'product-fact', product: product, key: 'wash_temp'
              endcapture
              assign care_cover_lc = care_cover | downcase
              assign care_derived = ''
              if care_cover_lc contains 'zip'
                if care_wash != ''
                  assign care_derived = 'product.accordion.care_zip_temp' | t: temp: care_wash
                else
                  assign care_derived = 'product.accordion.care_zip' | t
                endif
              elsif care_cover_lc contains 'coated'
                assign care_derived = 'product.accordion.care_coated' | t
              endif
            -%}
            {%- if care_mf != blank and care_mf.value != blank -%}
              {%- if care_mf.type == 'rich_text_field' -%}
                {{- care_mf | metafield_tag -}}
              {%- elsif care_mf.type contains 'list.' -%}
                <ul>{%- for c in care_mf.value -%}<li>{{ c | escape }}</li>{%- endfor -%}</ul>
              {%- else -%}
                <p>{{ care_mf.value | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif care_derived != '' -%}
              <p>{{ care_derived }}</p>
            {%- else -%}
              {{- extra -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- when 'page' -%}
            {%- if bs.page != blank -%}{{- bs.page.content -}}{%- endif -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {{- extra -}}
        {%- endcase -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign acc_body = acc_body | replace: '[trial_nights]', nights_s | replace: '[guarantee_years]', years_s | replace: '[threshold]', threshold_money | replace: '[trial_terms_short]', ph_terms_short | replace: '[trial_terms]', ph_terms -%}
      {%- if acc_body != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--accordion"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          <details class="accordion product-accordion"{% if bs.open %} open{% endif %}>
            <summary>
              <span class="product-accordion__title">
                {%- if bs.icon != blank and bs.icon != 'none' -%}
                  {%- render 'icon', name: bs.icon, class: 'product-accordion__icon' -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                <span>{{ bs.heading | default: product.title | escape }}</span>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="accordion__content rte">
              {{- acc_body -}}
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---------- Free text ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'text' -%}
      {%- if bs.text != blank -%}
        <div class="pblock pblock--text"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          <div class="rte buy-box__text buy-box__text--{{ bs.style | default: 'body' }}">
            {{- bs.text | replace: '[trial_nights]', nights_s | replace: '[guarantee_years]', years_s | replace: '[threshold]', threshold_money | replace: '[trial_terms_short]', ph_terms_short | replace: '[trial_terms]', ph_terms -}}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if compact -%}
  {%- if size_idx >= 0 and product.options_with_values[size_idx].values.size > 1 -%}
    {%- render 'size-guide', product: product, section: section, variant: current, compact: true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
